window.docContents[72].resolve({"/rules/RG1002/#RG1002-established":{"contents":"No owned declaration of the checked scope has sorryAx in its exact transitive axiom set.\n\nIt does not establish:\n\n* That the completed proof proves the intended statement; the proposition itself is reviewed against its intent.* Lean's own warning for sorry is a separate compiler diagnostic (RG2003); this rule does not depend on it, and disabling that warning does not waive this rule.\n\nReview obligations the rule-coverage map associates with this rule (identifiers of the checker's Residual account):\n\n* R-QUALIFY: the checker's detection is qualified for this invocation, toolchain and capability* R-INTENT: the proposition expresses the intended requirement, with its quantifiers, hypotheses and limits\n\nEvery accepted result lists all residual obligations as open, whatever rules it checked: R-INTENT, R-INVARIANT, R-LAWS, R-BOUNDARY, R-NONVACUITY, R-DOC, R-COST, R-QUALIFY (and R-GRAPH for a serialized-graph claim). A listed identifier is an open obligation, never a completed review.\n\nEvery accepted result also relies on these trusted mechanisms (the checker's Trusted account), which no rule verifies:\n\n* toolchain: Lean elaborator, kernel and compiler at the snapshot's toolchain identity* acquisition: manifest parsing, Lake loading, and source, configuration and dependency acquisition* extraction: environment extraction, compiler and worker processes, and JSON transport* runtime: native runtime and every execution boundary reported as trusted\n\n","context":"Regula rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009RG1002: Proof holes are forbidden","header":"What a passing result establishes","id":"/rules/RG1002/#RG1002-established"},"/rules/RG2001/#RG2001-established":{"contents":"A passing result was produced in the declared environment: Lake loaded the workspace with the exact toolchain and resolved dependency state the result reports. An unavailable or unidentified environment is incomplete and never accepted.\n\nIt does not establish:\n\n* That a dependency checkout matches its recorded revision's content: dependency acquisition is a trusted mechanism.* Anything about the source; no declaration was inspected.\n\nReview obligations the rule-coverage map associates with this rule (identifiers of the checker's Residual account):\n\n* R-QUALIFY: the checker's detection is qualified for this invocation, toolchain and capability\n\nEvery accepted result lists all residual obligations as open, whatever rules it checked: R-INTENT, R-INVARIANT, R-LAWS, R-BOUNDARY, R-NONVACUITY, R-DOC, R-COST, R-QUALIFY (and R-GRAPH for a serialized-graph claim). A listed identifier is an open obligation, never a completed review.\n\nEvery accepted result also relies on these trusted mechanisms (the checker's Trusted account), which no rule verifies:\n\n* toolchain: Lean elaborator, kernel and compiler at the snapshot's toolchain identity* acquisition: manifest parsing, Lake loading, and source, configuration and dependency acquisition* extraction: environment extraction, compiler and worker processes, and JSON transport* runtime: native runtime and every execution boundary reported as trusted\n\n","context":"Regula rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009RG2001: The declared Lean environment must be available","header":"What a passing result establishes","id":"/rules/RG2001/#RG2001-established"}});